1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,200
The app you use the most wasn't built to make you happy.

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:10,900
It was built to keep you here.

3
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:16,400
Stay till the end: there's a challenge that could change your next 7 days.

4
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:22,400
Every time you swipe, your brain places a bet: what if the next one is better?

5
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:28,400
Sometimes you get a like. Sometimes, nothing. And that's what hooks you.

6
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:35,600
The feed never ends. That's why you never feel satisfied.

7
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,550
Bad news.

8
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:39,150
Overdue bill.

9
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:41,050
Her perfect life.

10
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:42,150
One more like. One more. One more…

11
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:48,200
You compare your backstage to their spotlight.

12
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:49,851
And you lose.

13
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:53,800
Surrounded by people… and no one is there.

14
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:58,400
And when you finally put the phone down…

15
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:00,207
the silence screams.

16
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,200
The problem isn't the phone. It's the thirst.

17
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:25,200
Two thousand years ago, a woman went to draw water at noon, alone, so she wouldn't run into anyone.

18
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:31,000
At the well, there was Jesus. And He said:

19
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:43,200
“Whosoever drinketh of this water shall thirst again: but whosoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him shall never thirst.”

20
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:53,200
He wasn't talking about a well. He was talking about you.

21
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:02,000
You give the feed hours. He gave His life for you.

22
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:15,000
“God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.”

23
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:28,200
Not when you had it all together. When you were scrolling at three in the morning.

24
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:40,600
Instead of anxiety: peace. “The peace of God, which passeth all understanding.”

25
00:02:41,500 --> 00:02:53,200
Instead of exhaustion: rest. “Come unto me… and I will give you rest.”

26
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:05,600
Instead of comparison: identity. You are a son. You are a daughter of God.

27
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:18,200
Instead of loneliness: presence. “I will never leave thee, nor forsake thee.”

28
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:24,200
So here's my challenge to you.

29
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:34,000
For seven days, the first ten minutes of your morning, before your phone, belong to Him.

30
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:41,200
Open the Bible. Pray. Or just sit in silence with Him.

31
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:52,200
Comment “I'm in” if you're up for it. And send this to someone who needs to put the phone down today.
